      "transforms": [
        {
          "name": "decode",
          "expression": "ConeHalfAngle = abs(w); PDF = 1/abs(w); bIsFirstPersonPixel = (w < 0)",
          "requires": [
            "ReflectionRayBuffer"
          ],
          "sourceRefs": [
            "part2.refl.raydata.cone",
            "part2.refl.raydata.pdf",
            "part2.refl.raydata.fp"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "encode",
          "expression": "w = bIsFirstPerson ? -ConeHalfAngle : ConeHalfAngle, with ConeHalfAngle = max(1/max(Sample.PDF,1e-4), MinReflectionConeAngle)",
          "requires": [
            "ConeHalfAngle"
          ],
          "sourceRefs": [
            "part2.refl.ray.cone"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "mathTerms": [
        "MinReflectionConeAngle = 0.00001 (LumenReflectionCommon.ush:119); PDF is clamped to >= 0.0001 at LumenReflections.usf:362/387 before inversion.",
        "The 16-bit half storage quantizes both direction and cone angle; the direction is not renormalized after storage."
      ],
      "producerSources": [
        "part2.refl.cpp.raybuffer.create",
        "part2.refl.cpp.raybuffer.desc",
        "part2.refl.ray.write"
      ],
      "consumerSources": [
        "part2.refl.raydata.get"
      ],
      "gaps": [
        "There is no separate PDF channel: PDF is recovered as 1/|w|, so a stored 0 (or denormal) would produce an infinite PDF; the encode clamps ConeHalfAngle >= 1e-5, which bounds PDF <= 1e5."
      ],
